#. ~ Description of terrain "closed ballistic glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A ballistic glass door, consisting of layers of laminated glass."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "open ballistic glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A ballistic glass door, consisting of layers of laminated glass.  It's open."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up damaged reinforced door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A battered and torn reinforced door with planks bursting from the joints.  "
"The boarded up planks are fragmented and in pieces, this doesn't look like "
"an easy repair."
msgstr ""
"Poobijane i porozrywane wzmocnione drzwi z deskami wyrywającymi się ze "
"spoin. Zabarykadowane deski są połamane i w kawałkach, nie wygląda to na "
"łatwą naprawę."

#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A boarded up door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  "
"Although it's been covered up in planks, you could still look through the "
"peephole if you were close enough."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up damaged door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A boarded up wooden door, except that some of the planks are fractured or "
"coming loose.  Without repairs, it could be broken down easily."
msgstr ""
"Zabite deskami drewniane drzwi, z tym że niektóre deski pękają lub odpadają. "
"Bez napraw mogą być łatwo zniszczone."

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed laminated glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A closed door made of laminated safety glass.  It's a lot tougher than "
"regular glass, and is designed to break into fragments that are nowhere near "
"as sharp."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "open bar door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A detention door made up of crisscrossed stainless steel bars.  It's wide "
"open.  Freedom!"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed bar door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A detention door made up of crisscrossed stainless steel bars.  The locking "
"mechanism appears to be engaged.  You could pick it open with enough skill."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed bar door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A detention door made up of crisscrossed stainless steel bars.  The locking "
"mechanism doesn't appear to be engaged."
msgstr ""
"Drzwi celi zrobione z krzyżujących się nierdzewnych stalowych prętów. "
"Mechanizm ryglujący nie wydaje się być uruchomiony."

#. ~ Description of terrain "open laminated glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A door made of laminated safety glass.  It's a lot tougher than regular "
"glass, and is designed to break into fragments that are nowhere near as "
"sharp.  It's open."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A faux concrete wall positioned and joined seamlessly with the wall, this "
"wall is capable of resisting extreme elements as well as hostile forces.  "
"Blast load rated and extremely fire-retardant, breaching it will require "
"specialized tools or an industrial vehicle."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A galvanized steel door, forged to withstand punishment and impede anyone or "
"anything.  Typically used in conjunction with automated electronic locking "
"mechanisms that require an external source to unlock."
msgstr ""
"Galwanizowane stalowe drzwi, wykute by wytrzymać atak i zatrzymać "
"kogokolwiek i cokolwiek. Zwykle używane w połączeniu z automatycznymi "
"elektronicznymi zamkami wymagającymi zewnętrznych elementów odmykających."

#. ~ Description of terrain "open makeshift door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A makeshift screen consisting of planks bound together with rope, hanging "
"from the top of the doorway.  Could be easily taken down and re-purposed.  "
"The planks have been rolled up and attached to the top of the doorway, "
"allowing free movement through."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed makeshift door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A makeshift screen consisting of planks bound together with rope, hanging "
"vertically from the top of the doorway.  Could be easily taken down and re-"
"purposed."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A regular door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  If "
"you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the hole."
msgstr ""
"Zwykłe drewniane drzwi, z tym, że te mają wizjer. Jeśli je zbadasz "
"dokładnie, możesz zerknąć przez dziurkę."

#. ~ Description of terrain "open wood door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A regular door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  If "
"you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the hole.  No "
"need right now though, since the door is open anyway."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A regular door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  If "
"you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the hole.  This "
"one has a deadbolt keyhole, so it's likely locked.  You could pry it open or "
"pick the lock, or unlock the deadbolt from the inside."
msgstr ""
"Zwykłe drewniane drzwi, z tym, że te mają wizjer. Jeśli je zbadasz "
"dokładnie, możesz zerknąć przez dziurkę. Te zaopatrzono w zasuwkę, więc "
"pewnie są zamknięte. Możesz je wyważyć, spróbować otworzyć wytrychem lub "
"odryglować od środka."

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A regular door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  If "
"you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the hole.  This "
"one has a deadbolt numpad, so it's likely locked.  You could pry it open, "
"guessing the code is out of the question, or unlock the deadbolt from the "
"inside."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed frosted glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A sliding door of frosted white glass."
msgstr "Przesuwne drzwi z matowego białego szkła."

#. ~ Description of terrain "open glass door"
#. ~ Description of terrain "open frosted glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A sliding glass door that has been left open for all manner of things to "
"travel through."
msgstr "Przesuwne szklane drzwi otwarte na wszelki przechodzący ruch."

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A sliding glass door, clear enough that an animal or a particularly dumb "
"person could slam right into it.  This one is closed, so don't hurt yourself."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn "
"easily, too."
msgstr ""
"Standardowe drewniane drzwi, które nie wyglądają na zbyt wytrzymałe. "
"Prawdopodobnie łatwo się też palą."

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door with an electronic lock"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn "
"easily, too.  This one has a deadbolt electronic lock, so it's likely "
"locked.  You could pry it open, guessing the code is out of the question, or "
"unlock the deadbolt from the inside."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn "
"easily, too.  This one has a deadbolt keyhole, so it's likely locked.  You "
"could pry it open or pick the lock, or unlock the deadbolt from the inside."
msgstr ""
"Standardowe drewniane drzwi, które nie wyglądają na zbyt wytrzymałe. "
"Prawdopodobnie łatwo się też palą. Te zaopatrzono w zasuwkę, więc pewnie są "
"zamknięte. Możesz je wyważyć, spróbować otworzyć wytrychem lub odryglować od "
"środka."

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn "
"easily, too.  This one has an electronic keypad, so it's likely locked.  You "
"could pry it open, guessing the code is out of the question."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn "
"easily, too.  This one has an extra keyhole, so it's likely locked.  You "
"could pry it open or pick the lock."
msgstr ""
"Standardowe drewniane drzwi, które nie wyglądają na zbyt wytrzymałe. "
"Prawdopodobnie łatwo się też palą. Te zaopatrzono w zamek więc pewnie są "
"zamknięte na klucz. Możesz je wyważyć lub spróbować otworzyć zamek wytrychem."

#. ~ Description of terrain "open wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn "
"easily, too.  This one is wide open."
msgstr ""
"Standardowe drewniane drzwi, które nie wyglądają na zbyt wytrzymałe. "
"Prawdopodobnie łatwo się też palą. Te są otwarte na oścież."

#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that has several planks across it, nailed down to "
"board it up and increase its durability.  It's still flammable, though."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed corrugated metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A thin door made of corrugated steel held in a frame."
msgstr "Cienkie drzwi wykonane z blachy falistej trzymane w ramie."

#. ~ Description of terrain "open corrugated metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A thin door made of corrugated steel held in a frame.  It's open, so no "
"tools are needed to break in."
msgstr ""
"Cienkie drzwi wykonane z blachy falistej, osadzone w ramie. Są otwarte, więc "
"do włamania nie potrzeba żadnych narzędzi."

#. ~ Description of terrain "damaged wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A trashed wooden door, with a large hole in the middle that you can see "
"right through.  The doorknob is so messed up that it can't be opened "
"anymore.  It could be fixed up with a few planks."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up damaged door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"A wrecked door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole and "
"some partly-splintered boards nailed across it.  The peephole is damaged and "
"can't be used to see through."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up reinforced door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An additionally reinforced door of layered planks that has been boarded up "
"with more wood to prevent it from opening.  It's still susceptible to fire."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "empty door frame"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An empty door frame made from planks and nails.  A variety of doors could be "
"constructed here."
msgstr ""
"Pusta ościeżnica wykonana z desek i gwoździ. Można tu zbudować wiele różnych "
"drzwi."

#. ~ Description of terrain "empty metal door frame"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An empty door frame made of steel and assorted metal.  A variety of doors "
"could be constructed here."
msgstr ""
"Pusta ościeżnica ze stali i innych metali. Można tu zamontować różne rodzaje "
"drzwi."

#. ~ Description of terrain "empty metal window frame"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An empty window frame constructed from assembled metal and carefully braced "
"with various hardware."
msgstr "Pusta futryna z metalu ostrożnie osadzona za pomocą narzędzi."

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape."
msgstr ""
"Niezwykle wytrzymałe drzwi zrobione ze stalowych elementów dociętych i "
"zbitych ze sobą na wymiar."

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  If you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the "
"peephole."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "electronic locked metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  It is locked by an electronic keypad."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "open metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  It's open, so no tools are needed to break in."
msgstr ""
"Niezwykle wytrzymałe drzwi zrobione ze stalowych elementów dociętych i "
"zbitych ze sobą na wymiar. Są otwarte, więc nie potrzeba narzędzi, by się "
"włamywać."

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  This one has an extra keyhole, so it's likely locked.  You could "
"probably pick the lock."
msgstr ""
"Niezwykle wytrzymałe drzwi zrobione ze stalowych elementów dociętych i "
"zbitych ze sobą na wymiar. Te mają zamek, więc są prawdopodobnie zamknięte. "
"Prawdopodobnie można by spróbować wytrycha na zamku."

#. ~ Description of terrain "open metal door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, cut and pounded into "
"shape.  If you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the "
"peephole.  No need right now though, since the door is open anyway."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed bulkhead door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of cast metal, it is watertight and opened "
"using the fly wheel."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "open bulkhead door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of cast metal, it is watertight, or would "
"be if it was closed."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"An industrially fabricated thick sheet carefully positioned and joined "
"seamlessly with perimeter sealant, this wall is capable of resisting extreme "
"elements as well as hostile forces.  Blast load rated and extremely fire-"
"retardant, breaching it will require specialized tools or an industrial "
"vehicle."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "open lighthouse lens hinged section"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An intricate arrangement of glass, designed to focus light from within to be "
"visible over long distances.  This section of the lens is hinged and is "
"currently open."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed lighthouse lens hinged section"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"An intricate arrangement of glass, designed to focus light from within to be "
"visible over long distances.  This section of the lens is on hinges and can "
"be opened for maintenance."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "damaged reinforced wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"Despite someone's best efforts at reinforcing this door, there are "
"splintering planks and visible holes in the wood, it could soon be smashed "
"apart completely if not repaired.  The doorknob is all messed up and the "
"door can't be opened until it's fixed."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed reinforced wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"Just like other wooden doors, except this one has layers of nailed-on planks "
"and an additional hinge for reinforcement.  It might be barricaded, but it's "
"still susceptible to fire."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "open reinforced wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"Just like other wooden doors, except this one has layers of nailed-on planks "
"for reinforcement.  It might be fortified, but it's still susceptible to "
"fire.  It's open, so it's not stopping anything right now."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed door curtain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"Repurposed curtains from a window covering a door frame.  Could be easily "
"taken down for supplies or placed somewhere else."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "open door curtain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"Repurposed curtains from a window covering a door frame.  Could be easily "
"taken down for supplies or placed somewhere else.  The curtains are open, "
"bundled, and tied next to the doorway."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed grass curtain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"Sheets of grass yarn covering a door frame.  Could be easily taken down for "
"supplies or placed somewhere else."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "open grass curtain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"Sheets of grass yarn covering a door frame.  Could be easily taken down for "
"supplies or placed somewhere else.  The curtains are open, bundled, and tied "
"next to the doorway."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "damaged wood door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"The bad news is that the peephole is broken and you can't use it to look "
"through the door.  The good news is that the door is nearly broken down, so "
"there's nothing blocking the view.  Also, the doorknob is so messed up that "
"it can't be opened anymore.  A few planks, nails, and the right tools could "
"patch up all the damage."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain "closed bar door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "The door swings open…"
msgstr "Drzwi otwierają się…"

#. ~ Prying failure of terrain ""
#. ~ Prying failure of terrain "closed metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "The metal door is too thick."
msgstr "Metalowe drzwi są za grube."

#. ~ Description of terrain "open secret door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"This apparently normal segment of concrete wall has opened to reveal a "
"secret passage."
msgstr ""
"Ten pozornie normalny fragment betonowej ściany otworzył się, odsłaniając "
"tajne przejście."

#. ~ Description of terrain "open secret door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid ""
"This apparently normal segment of metal wall has opened to reveal a secret "
"passage."
msgstr ""
"Ten pozornie normalny fragment metalowej ściany otworzył się, odsłaniając "
"tajne przejście."

#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain "closed wood door"
#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain ""
#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain "closed metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "With a satisfying click, the lock on the door opens."
msgstr "Z satysfakcjonującym kliknięciem, zamek w drzwiach otwiera się."

#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "closed bar door"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "locked wire gate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "closed wire gate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "open wire gate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "locked retractable gate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "closed retractable gate"
