#. ~ Description of terrain "grape bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A bush of a different species invaded by grape vines, but they're fruitless."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "grape bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A bush of a different species invaded by grape vines."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "spicebush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A bush that features small, red berries."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "spicebush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A bush that usually features small, red berries but it was picked clean."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A dead tree that has lost most all of its smaller branches."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A dead tree.  It either hasn't been dead long or it's sat undisturbed, it "
"still has most of its branches."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "alder tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous flowering tree with serrated, scalloped, round-obovate leaves, "
"commonly forming dense groves alongside water."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "pistachio tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the 'Pistacia' genus.  This is a cultivated tree, and is "
"not native to this region.  Unfortunately, it looks like it has been picked "
"clean of pistachio nuts."
msgstr ""
"Drzewo liściaste z rodzaju „Pistacia”. Jest to drzewo uprawne i nie "
"występuje w tym regionie. Niestety, wygląda na to, że zostało oskubane z "
"orzechów pistacjowych."

#. ~ Description of terrain "pistachio tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the 'Pistacia' genus.  This is a cultivated tree, and is "
"not native to this region.  You could look for pistachio nuts if you "
"examined the tree more closely."
msgstr ""
"Drzewo liściaste z rodzaju „Pistacia”. Jest to drzewo uprawne, które nie "
"występuje w tym regionie. Po dokładniejszym zbadaniu drzewa można by "
"poszukać orzechów pistacjowych."

#. ~ Description of terrain "almond tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the 'Prunus' genus.  This is a cultivated tree, and is "
"not native to this region.  There are no almonds left to pick on the tree."
msgstr ""
"Drzewo liściaste z rodzaju „Prunus”. Jest to drzewo uprawne, które nie "
"występuje w tym regionie. Na tym drzewie nie ma już migdałów do zebrania."

#. ~ Description of terrain "almond tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the 'Prunus' genus.  This is a cultivated tree, and is "
"not native to this region.  You could look for fresh almonds if you examined "
"the tree more closely."
msgstr ""
"Drzewo liściaste z rodzaju „Prunus”. Jest to drzewo uprawne, które nie "
"występuje w tym regionie. Po bliższym przyjrzeniu się drzewu można by "
"poszukać świeżych migdałów."

#. ~ Description of terrain "blackjack oak"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the genus 'Quercus', with bark cracked into rectangular "
"black plates split by narrow orange fissures.  All the usable bark has been "
"stripped off."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "blackjack oak"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the genus 'Quercus', with bark cracked into rectangular "
"black plates split by narrow orange fissures.  You could peel off the bark "
"sections if you examined the tree more closely."
msgstr ""
"Drzewo liściaste z rodzaju „Quercus”, z korą spękaną w prostokątne czarne "
"płytki, poprzecinane wąskimi pomarańczowymi szczelinami. Po dokładniejszym "
"przyjrzeniu się drzewu można by zedrzeć fragmenty kory."

#. ~ Description of terrain "hydrangea bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A dense bush of fragrant blue hydrangeas."
msgstr "Gęsty krzew pachnących niebieskich hortensji."

#. ~ Description of terrain "underbrush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A dense patch of vegetation.  Foraging here could turn up all sorts of "
"things, and would be a bit faster with a tool for cutting plants."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "underbrush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A dense patch of vegetation.  It has been rummaged through and doesn't have "
"anything useful left to forage from it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "rose bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A fat bush of beautiful red roses, if only you could get a date!  Watch out "
"for its thorns!"
msgstr ""
"Okrągły krzew ślicznych czerwonych róż; świetnych na randkę gdybyś ją miał "
"mieć. Uwaga na kolce!"

#. ~ Description of terrain "hydrangea bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A fat hydrangea bush that currently has no blooms."
msgstr "Okrągły krzew hortensji, obecnie bez kwiatów."

#. ~ Description of terrain "rose bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A fat rose bush that currently has no blooms.  Watch out for its thorns!"
msgstr "Okrągły krzew róż, obecnie bez kwiatów. Uwaga na kolce!"

#. ~ Description of terrain "mega fern"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A gigantic fern like nothing you've seen before.  The leaves are a bright "
"scarlet with a net-like structure of green veins.  The multipronged trunks "
"have the texture of balsa wood."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "bee hive"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A hive of bees located in a cavity inside a tree, swarming in and out at a "
"feverish pace.  There's probably honey inside."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "maple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A large deciduous tree of the 'Acer' genus.  The leaves are distinctively "
"shaped with five prongs.  A spigot is wedged into the trunk, and sweet maple "
"sap can be extracted."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "maple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A large deciduous tree of the 'Acer' genus.  The leaves are distinctively "
"shaped with five prongs.  It could be tapped in order to extract maple sap."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "mushroom colony"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A large pile of organic matter which has molded over with fungus.  The caps "
"of many ordinary mushrooms spring from the top, though these are woody and "
"clearly inedible."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "cottonwood tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A large tree belonging to the 'Populus' genus, commonly found throughout the "
"New England region.  All the cottonwood tree bolls have been harvested."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "cottonwood tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A large tree belonging to the 'Populus' genus, commonly found throughout the "
"New England region.  You see some cottonwood tree bolls that can be "
"harvested."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "elm tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A large tree belonging to the 'Ulmus' genus, commonly found throughout the "
"New England region."
msgstr ""
"Duże drzewo drzewo należące do rodzaju „Ulmus”, typowo rosnące na terenach "
"Nowej Anglii."

#. ~ Description of terrain "sycamore tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A long-lived tree with flaky bark and a broad trunk."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "apiary"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A man-made wooden box designed to hold honeybees and facilitate the care for "
"a hive.  The modular construction allows for inspecting the bees and "
"harvesting their bounty without destroying the hive completely.  This year's "
"harvest should be ready by now."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "apiary"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A man-made wooden box designed to host honeybees and facilitate the care for "
"a hive.  The modular construction allows for inspecting the bees and "
"harvesting their bounty without destroying the hive completely.  It will be "
"some time before this one is ready to harvest."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "oak tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive deciduous tree belonging to the 'Quercus' genus, commonly found "
"throughout the New England region."
msgstr ""
"Masywne rozłożyste drzewo należące do rodzaju „Quercus” (dąb), typowo "
"rosnące na terenach Nowej Anglii."

#. ~ Description of terrain "oak tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive deciduous tree belonging to the 'Quercus' genus, commonly found "
"throughout the New England region.  If you look closely, you can see some "
"acorns the squirrels haven't gotten yet."
msgstr ""
"Masywne rozłożyste drzewo należące do rodzaju „Quercus” (dąb), typowo "
"rosnące na terenach Nowej Anglii. Jeśli spojrzysz uważnie, zauważysz "
"żołędzie, do których jeszcze nie dobrały się wiewiórki."

#. ~ Description of terrain "chestnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A massive tree belonging to the 'Castanea' genus."
msgstr "Masywne rozłożyste drzewo należące do gatunku „Castanea”."

#. ~ Description of terrain "chestnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive tree belonging to the 'Castanea' genus.  If you look closely, you "
"can see some unharvested chestnuts."
msgstr ""
"Masywne rozłożyste drzewo należące do gatunku „Castanea”. Gdy przyjrzysz się "
"uważnie zobaczysz nie zebrane kasztany."

#. ~ Description of terrain "beech tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A massive tree belonging to the 'Fagus' genus."
msgstr "Masywne rozłożyste drzewo należące do gatunku „Fagus”."

#. ~ Description of terrain "beech tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive tree belonging to the 'Fagus' genus.  If you look closely, you can "
"see some unharvested beech nuts."
msgstr ""
"Masywne rozłożyste drzewo należące do gatunku „Fagus”. Gdy przyjrzysz się "
"uważnie zobaczysz nie zebrane bukwie."

#. ~ Description of terrain "butternut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive tree belonging to the 'Juglans' genus, but with lighter bark and "
"more elongated fruits than the more common black walnut."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "butternut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive tree belonging to the 'Juglans' genus, but with lighter bark and "
"more elongated fruits than the more common black walnut.  If you look "
"closely, you can see some unharvested butternuts."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "walnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A massive tree belonging to the 'Juglans' genus."
msgstr "Masywne rozłożyste drzewo należące do gatunku „Juglans”."

#. ~ Description of terrain "walnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive tree belonging to the 'Juglans' genus.  If you look closely, you "
"can see some unharvested walnuts."
msgstr ""
"Masywne rozłożyste drzewo należące do gatunku „Juglans”. Gdy przyjrzysz się "
"uważnie zobaczysz nie zebrane orzechy."

#. ~ Description of terrain "ash tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A member of the 'Fraxinus' genus, these hardwood trees have long been prized "
"for their lumber."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "young tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A relatively young sapling of an indeterminate species.  It could take "
"decades before reaching maturity, so there's no use waiting around."
msgstr ""
"Stosunkowo młoda sadzonka drzewa nieidentyfikowalnego gatunku. Wzrost do "
"dorosłości może potrwać dekady, więc nie ma na co czekać."

#. ~ Description of terrain "tree trunk"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A section of trunk from a tree that has been cut down.  Can be sawn into "
"logs with the right tool."
msgstr ""
"Część pnia drzewa, które zostało ścięte. Przy pomocy odpowiedniego narzędzia "
"może być pocięty na kłody."

#. ~ Description of terrain "fern"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A short plant with thousands of leaves which grow in a fractal pattern from "
"the stem."
msgstr ""
"Krótka roślina z tysiącami liści, które wyrastają w fraktalny wzór z łodygi."

#. ~ Description of terrain "fern"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A short plant with thousands of leaves which grow in a fractal pattern.  All "
"of the curled shoots have been harvested."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "blackberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small blackberry bush that's fruitless.  Watch out for its thorns!"
msgstr "Mały krzak jeżyn, bez owoców. Uwaga na kolce!"

#. ~ Description of terrain "blueberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small blueberry bush that's fruitless."
msgstr "Mały krzak borówek, bez owoców."

#. ~ Description of terrain "peanut bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small bush of crunchy peanuts."
msgstr "Mały krzak z kłączami pełnymi chrupiących orzeszków ziemnych."

#. ~ Description of terrain "blackberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small bush of delicious blackberries.  Watch out for its thorns!"
msgstr "Mały krzak smacznych jeżyn. Uwaga na kolce!"

#. ~ Description of terrain "raspberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small bush of delicious raspberries.  Watch out for its thorns!"
msgstr "Mały krzak smacznych malin. Uwaga na kolce!"

#. ~ Description of terrain "huckleberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small bush of huckleberries, often mistaken for blueberries."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "strawberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small bush of juicy strawberries."
msgstr "Mały krzak soczystych truskawek."

#. ~ Description of terrain "blueberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small bush of sweet blueberries."
msgstr "Mały krzak słodkich jagód."

#. ~ Description of terrain "huckleberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small huckleberry bush that's fruitless."
msgstr "Mały krzak borówki amerykańskiej, bez owoców."

#. ~ Description of terrain "peanut bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small peanut bush that's fruitless."
msgstr "Mały krzak orzeszków ziemnych, który nie ma owoców."

#. ~ Description of terrain "golf hole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small plastic cup embedded in an area of very short, neat grass."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "raspberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small raspberry bush that's fruitless.  Watch out for its thorns!"
msgstr "Mały krzak malin, bez owoców. Uwaga na kolce!"

#. ~ Description of terrain "shrub"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small shrub."
msgstr "Mały krzew."

#. ~ Description of terrain "strawberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small strawberry bush that's fruitless."
msgstr "Mały krzak truskawek, bez owoców."

#. ~ Description of terrain "hazelnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A stubby tree belonging to the 'Corylus' genus."
msgstr "Przysadziste drzewo należące do rodzaju „Corylus”."

#. ~ Description of terrain "hazelnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A stubby tree belonging to the 'Corylus' genus.  If you look closely, you "
"can see some unharvested hazelnuts."
msgstr ""
"Przysadziste drzewo należące do rodzaju „Corylus”. Gdy przyjrzysz się "
"uważnie zobaczysz nie zebrane orzechy laskowe."

#. ~ Description of terrain "tall bamboo"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A tall bamboo thicket about head high."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "birch tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Betula' genus, with the characteristic peeling "
"bark.  Species like 'B. alleghaniensis', 'B. papyrifera', and 'B. "
"populifolia' are the most common in the New England region.  Looks like "
"there isn't enough rhytidome to peel off yet."
msgstr ""
"Wysokie drzewo liściaste z rodzaju „Betula”, z charakterystyczną łuszczącą "
"się korą. Gatunki takie jak „B. alleghaniensis”, „B. papyrifera” i „B. "
"populifolia” są najczęstsze w rejonie Nowej Anglii. Wygląda na to, że nie ma "
"na tyle kory by ją zedrzeć."

#. ~ Description of terrain "birch tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Betula' genus, with the characteristic peeling "
"bark.  Species like 'B. alleghaniensis', 'B. papyrifera', and 'B. "
"populifolia' are the most common in the New England region.  You could tear "
"off some strips of bark if you examined the tree more closely."
msgstr ""
"Wysokie drzewo liściaste z rodzaju „Betula”, z charakterystyczną łuszczącą "
"się korą. Gatunki takie jak „B. alleghaniensis”, „B. papyrifera” i „B. "
"populifolia” są najczęstsze w rejonie Nowej Anglii. Możesz zedrzeć nieco "
"kory, jeśli obejrzysz drzewo dokładniej."

#. ~ Description of terrain "pecan tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  It doesn't look like there are "
"any pecan nuts left on the tree."
msgstr ""
"Wysokie drzewo liściaste z rodzaju „Carya”. Nie wygląda na to, żeby na "
"drzewie pozostały jakieś orzechy."

#. ~ Description of terrain "hickory tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  It looks like the tree has been "
"picked clean of hickory nuts."
msgstr ""
"Wysokie drzewo liściaste z rodzaju „Carya”. Wygląda na to, że drzewo zostało "
"oskubane z orzechów."

#. ~ Description of terrain "hickory tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  You could look for hickory nuts "
"if you examined the tree more closely."
msgstr ""
"Wysokie drzewo liściaste z rodzaju „Carya”. Po dokładniejszym zbadaniu "
"drzewa można by szukać orzechów."

#. ~ Description of terrain "pecan tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  You could look for pecan nuts "
"if you examined the tree more closely."
msgstr ""
"Wysokie drzewo liściaste z rodzaju „Carya”. Po dokładniejszym zbadaniu "
"drzewa można by szukać orzechów pekan."

#. ~ Description of terrain "willow tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall, wide deciduous tree of the 'Salix' genus, with long, thin, leafy "
"branches that hang down like curtains.  Looks like all usable bark has been "
"torn off, and new rhytidomes have not formed yet."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "willow tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall, wide deciduous tree of the 'Salix' genus, with long, thin, leafy "
"branches that hang down like curtains.  You could tear off some bark."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "pine tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A towering coniferous tree that belongs to the 'Pinus' genus, with the New "
"England species varying from 'P. strobus', 'P. resinosa' and 'P. rigida'.  "
"If you examined the tree more closely, you might find usable sticky whorls, "
"resin clumps, and pinecones."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "pine tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A towering coniferous tree that belongs to the 'Pinus' genus, with the New "
"England species varying from 'P. strobus', 'P. resinosa' and 'P. rigida'.  "
"Some of the branches and resin clumps have been stripped away and many of "
"the pinecones aren't developed fully yet, but given a season, it could be "
"harvestable again."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead pine tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A towering coniferous tree that belongs to the 'Pinus' genus, with the New "
"England species varying from 'P. strobus', 'P. resinosa' and 'P. rigida'.  "
"This tree's branches are bare, and it appears to be dead."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "apricot tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A transplanted species of 'Prunus armeniaca', rarely found in New England.  "
"It produces apricots in the summer.  If you examined the spurs more closely, "
"you could probably find some mature apricots."
msgstr ""
"Szczepiony gatunek „Prunus armeniaca” rzadko spotykany w Nowej Anglii. Latem "
"owocuje morelami. Bo zbadaniu gałęzi możesz pewnie znaleźć kilka "
"dojrzalszych morel."

#. ~ Description of terrain "apricot tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A transplanted species of 'Prunus armeniaca', rarely found in New England.  "
"It produces apricots in the summer.  Looks like all the ripe apricots have "
"been picked."
msgstr ""
"Szczepiony gatunek „Prunus armeniaca” rzadko spotykany w Nowej Anglii. Latem "
"owocuje morelami. Dojrzałe morele zostały już niestety zebrane."

#. ~ Description of terrain "tree stump"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A tree stump, a remnant of a tree that has been cut down."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "lilac bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A wide bush of bright pinkish-purple lilacs."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "lilac bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A wide lilac bush that currently has no blooms."
msgstr "Rozłożysty krzew bzu, który obecnie nie kwitnie."

#. ~ Description of terrain "shorn grass"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of grass clipped nearly down to the roots."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "white grass"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"An area of grass covered in white latex-based paint, with neat lines "
"designed for recreational sports."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "golf green"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of grass mowed very short and neat."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "grass"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of hardy grass about ankle high."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "long bamboo shoots"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of long bamboo shoots about shin high."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead bamboo"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of long, brown, dead bamboo shoots covered in white fungus."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "long grass"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of long, shaggy grass about shin high."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "tall grass"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of tall grass about head high."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "young bamboo shoots"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"An area of young bamboo shoots about ankle high.  Many shoots are just "
"barely pushing above the ground."
msgstr ""
"Obszar z młodymi pędami bambusa o wysokości około kostki. Wiele pędów ledwo "
"wystaje ponad ziemię."

#. ~ Description of terrain "young bamboo shoots"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"An area of young bamboo shoots about ankle high.  The smallest shoots have "
"already been harvested."
msgstr ""
"Obszar z młodymi pędami bambusa o wysokości około kostki. Najmniejsze pędy "
"zostały już zebrane."

#. ~ Description of terrain "autumn olive"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"An invasive species from Japan which is also called silverberry.  Widely "
"planted in the 1940s to combat erosion, it spread far and wide, often even "
"displacing native plants.  As it name says, it bears fruits in autumn, which "
"are quite unlike olives, but this particular plant has been harvested "
"already."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "autumn olive"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"An invasive species from Japan which is also called silverberry.  Widely "
"planted in the 1940s to combat erosion, it spread far and wide, often even "
"displacing native plants.  As it name says, it bears fruits in autumn, which "
"are quite unlike olives."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "hobblebush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"Called hobblebush because it may hinder and trip, hobbles, unwary hikers "
"with its branches bending over and taking root.  It also bears surprisingly "
"sweet berries in autumn, if it hadn't been picked clean already."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "hobblebush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"Called hobblebush because it may hinder and trip, hobbles, unwary hikers "
"with its branches bending over and taking root.  It also bears surprisingly "
"sweet berries in autumn."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "black chokeberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"Drooping black berries adorn the shrub during autumn.  These have a "
"distinctive star-shaped fold and look quite juicy."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "black chokeberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"Drooping black berries adorned this shrub, but the shrub was picked clean."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "tupelo tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"Its name, originating from Native American tongues and garbled by the "
"settlers, approximately means \"swamp tree\".  During autumn it bears cherry-"
"like fruits, but someone picked this one clean already."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "tupelo tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"Its name, originating from Native American tongues and garbled by the "
"settlers, approximately means \"swamp tree\".  During autumn it bears cherry-"
"like fruits."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "cherry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it bears "
"cherries in the summer.  If you examined the foliage more closely, you could "
"probably find some viable clusters."
msgstr ""
"Jeden z licznych gatunków drzew „Prunus” rosnących w Nowej Anglii, rodzących "
"wiśnie w lecie. Bo zbadaniu listowia możesz pewnie znaleźć kilka nadających "
"się do spożycia kiści."

#. ~ Description of terrain "cherry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it bears "
"cherries in the summer.  Looks like all the ripe bunches of cherries have "
"been picked."
msgstr ""
"Jeden z licznych gatunków drzew „Prunus” rosnących w Nowej Anglii, rodzących "
"wiśnie w lecie. Dojrzałe wiśnie zostały już najwyraźniej zebrane."

#. ~ Description of terrain "peach tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it bears "
"peaches in the summer.  If you examined the branches more closely, you could "
"probably find some mature peaches."
msgstr ""
"Jeden z licznych gatunków drzew „Prunus” rosnących w Nowej Anglii, rodzących "
"brzoskwinie w lecie. Bo zbadaniu gałęzi możesz pewnie znaleźć kilka "
"dojrzalszych brzoskwinek."

#. ~ Description of terrain "peach tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it bears "
"peaches in the summer.  Looks like all the ripe peaches have been picked."
msgstr ""
"Jeden z licznych gatunków drzew „Prunus” rosnących w Nowej Anglii, rodzących "
"brzoskwinie w lecie. Dojrzałe brzoskwinie zostały już niestety zebrane."

#. ~ Description of terrain "plum tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it "
"produces plums in the summer.  If you examined the spurs more closely, you "
"could probably find some ripe plums."
msgstr ""
"Jeden z licznych gatunków drzew „Prunus” rosnących w Nowej Anglii, rodzących "
"śliwki w lecie. Bo zbadaniu gałęzi możesz pewnie znaleźć kilka dojrzalszych "
"śliwek."

#. ~ Description of terrain "plum tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it "
"produces plums in the summer.  Looks like all the ripe plums have been "
"picked."
msgstr ""
"Jeden z licznych gatunków drzew „Prunus” rosnących w Nowej Anglii, rodzących "
"śliwki w lecie. Dojrzałe śliwki zostały już niestety zebrane."

#. ~ Description of terrain "juniper tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the species of 'Juniperus' that grows in New England, juniper berries "
"grow over two to three years.  It flowers in the first year, produces a "
"green berry the second, and in the third produces the more famed blue "
"varieties.  If you examined the foliage more closely, you could probably "
"find some viable clusters."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "juniper tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the species of 'Juniperus' that grows in New England, juniper berries "
"grow over two to three years.  It flowers in the first year, produces a "
"green berry the second, and in the third produces the more famed blue "
"varieties.  Looks like all the ripe bunches of berries have been picked."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "magnolia tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"Part of an ancient lineage of broadleaf trees known for their large white "
"flowers."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead grass"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "Patchy grass which has withered and died."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "woodchips"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"Small splinters of wood laid out in a layer to prevent unwanted plants from "
"growing."
msgstr ""
"Warstwa małych ścinków drewna wysypanych by zapobiec wzrostowi niechcianych "
"roślin."

#. ~ Description of terrain "basswood tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"The American linden.  It has pretty and sweet-smelling flowers in the "
"summer, and its edible young leaves have already been harvested."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "basswood tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"The American linden.  It has pretty and sweet-smelling flowers in the "
"summer, and you might be able to eat its young leaves in the spring."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "warped dead pine tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"The branches of this pine tree have been twisted into a shape that remind "
"you of Sierpinski triangles.  It did not survive being warped like this."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead hickory tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"The dead remnants of a tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  Nothing "
"useful can be foraged from this poor, dead tree."
msgstr ""
"Martwe szczątki wysokiego drzewa liściastego z rodzaju „Carya”. Z tego "
"biednego, martwego drzewa nie da się zebrać nic pożytecznego."

#. ~ Description of terrain "sweet birch tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"The sweet birch lacks the paper bark of its cousins in the 'Betula' genus.  "
"It gets its name from its sweet sap, which can be tapped with a spile and "
"used to make syrup."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "sweet birch tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"The sweet birch lacks the paper bark of its cousins in the 'Betula' genus.  "
"This one's tapped with a spile."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "warped dead tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This deciduous tree's branches are warped into a spiral.  This appears to "
"have killed it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "coffee tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This is 'Gymnocladus dioicus', or the Kentucky coffee tree, which produces "
"roastable coffee pods and brewable leaves in the fall.  If you examined the "
"branches more closely, you could probably find a few mature ones."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "coffee tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This is 'Gymnocladus dioicus', or the Kentucky coffee tree, which produces "
"roastable coffee pods and brewable leaves in the fall.  Looks like all the "
"ripe pods have been picked."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "pear tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This is 'Pyrus communis', or the common pear tree, which produces fruit in "
"the fall.  If you examined the branches more closely, you could probably "
"find a few mature ones."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "pear tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This is 'Pyrus communis', or the common pear tree, which produces fruit in "
"the fall.  Looks like all the ripe pears have been picked."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "hemlock tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This is an evergreen tree from the 'Tsuga' genus, superficially similar to a "
"pine."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "hemlock tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This is an evergreen tree from the 'Tsuga' genus, superficially similar to a "
"pine.  Some of the branches and resin clumps have been stripped away and "
"many of the cones aren't developed fully yet, but given a season, it could "
"be harvestable again."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "nannyberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This small tree, it could almost be a large shrub, bears clusters of dark "
"blue berries in autumn, but someone picked this one clean already."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "nannyberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This small tree, it could almost be a large shrub, bears clusters of dark "
"blue berries in autumn."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "apple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Malus' genus, producing fruit commonly known "
"as apples.  If you examined the branches more closely, you could probably "
"find a few mature ones in autumn."
msgstr ""
"To drzewo należy do rodzaju „Malus” i rodzi owoce zwane powszechnie "
"jabłkami. Po dokładniejszym zbadaniu znalazło by się pewnie kilka dojrzałych "
"w okresie jesieni."

#. ~ Description of terrain "apple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Malus' genus, producing fruit commonly known "
"as apples.  There do not appear to be any ripe apples now."
msgstr ""
"To drzewo należy do rodzaju „Malus” i rodzi owoce zwane powszechnie "
"jabłkami. Nie wygląda na to, by obecnie były na nim jakiekolwiek dojrzałe "
"jabłuszka."

#. ~ Description of terrain "crabapple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Malus' genus, though unlike popular cultivars, "
"its fruits are small and sour.  If you examined the branches more closely, "
"you could probably find a few mature ones in autumn."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "crabapple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Malus' genus, though unlike popular cultivars, "
"its fruits are small and sour.  There do not appear to be any ripe "
"crabapples now."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "mulberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Morus' genus, producing fruit commonly known "
"as mulberries.  In the summer, many berries can be picked."
msgstr ""
"To drzewo należy do rodzaju „Morus” i rodzi owoce zwane powszechnie jagodami "
"morwy. W lecie można nazbierać sporo takich jagód."

#. ~ Description of terrain "mulberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Morus' genus, producing fruit commonly known "
"as mulberries.  There do not appear to be any ripe mulberries now."
msgstr ""
"To drzewo należy do rodzaju „Morus” i rodzi owoce zwane powszechnie jagodami "
"morwy. Nie wygląda na to, by obecnie były na nim jakiekolwiek dojrzałe owoce."

#. ~ Description of terrain "elderberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Sambucus' genus, producing fruit commonly "
"known as elderberries.  In the summer, many berries can be picked."
msgstr ""
"To drzewo należy do rodzaju „Sambucus” i rodzi owoce zwane powszechnie "
"jagodami dzikiego bzu. W lecie można nazbierać sporo takich jagód."

#. ~ Description of terrain "elderberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Sambucus' genus, producing fruit commonly "
"known as elderberries.  There do not appear to be any ripe elderberries now."
msgstr ""
"To drzewo należy do rodzaju „Sambucus” i rodzi owoce zwane powszechnie "
"jagodami dzikiego bzu. Nie wygląda na to, by obecnie były na nim "
"jakiekolwiek dojrzałe owoce."

#. ~ Description of terrain "sassafras tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Sassafras' genus, known for its aromatic "
"qualities.  In the winter and spring, the sap rich roots can be harvested to "
"make a sweet beverage."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "sassafras tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Sassafras' genus, known for its aromatic "
"qualities.  This tree's roots have been harvested, any more and the tree "
"will die."
msgstr ""

