#. ~ Description of "large cattle fodder bundle"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A big heap of cattle fodder, enough to feed a cow for a day."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "earthworm"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A common earthworm."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "boiled earthworms"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A handful of common earthworms, boiled to remove impurities."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "fried earthworms"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A handful of fried earthworms, cooked in salt."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cooked beans"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A hearty serving of cooked beans."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "chunk of beeswax"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A large chunk of beeswax.  Despite being used in some cooking recipes, "
"beeswax in itself is indigestible to humans."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "honey comb"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A large chunk of wax filled with honey.  Very tasty."
msgstr "Duży kawałek wosku pszczelego wypełnionego miodem. Bardzo smaczny."

#. ~ Description of "slime glob"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A little hunk of glop that fell off a slime monster.  It doesn't seem "
"hostile, but it does wiggle occasionally."
msgstr ""
"Mała pacyna żelatynowego śluzu z glutowego potwora. Nie wygląda na wrogo "
"nastawioną, ale trzęsie się od czasu do czasu."

#. ~ Description of "seed paste"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A mass of ground seeds that are ready to be pressed into oil."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "napkin"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A napkin.  Can be used for fires."
msgstr "Serwetka. Może się nadać do rozniecenia ognia."

#. ~ Description of "chamomile tea bag"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A paper sachet with dried chamomile inside.  Put it into boiling water to "
"make a cup of chamomile tea."
msgstr ""
"Papierowa saszetka z suszonym rumiankiem w środku. Włóż do wrzątku, by "
"przygotować kubek rumiankowej herbaty."

#. ~ Description of "dandelion tea bag"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A paper sachet with dried dandelion roots inside.  Put it into boiling water "
"to make a cup of dandelion tea."
msgstr ""
"Papierowa saszetka z suszonymi mleczami w środku. Włóż do wrzątku, by "
"przygotować kubek herbaty z mleczy."

#. ~ Description of "herbal tea bag"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A paper sachet with dried wild herbs inside.  Put it into boiling water to "
"make a cup of herbal tea."
msgstr ""
"Papierowa saszetka z suszonymi ziołami w środku. Włóż do wrzątku, by "
"przygotować kubek ziołowej herbaty."

#. ~ Description of "fruit tea bag"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A paper sachet with leaves and fruit parts inside.  Put it into boiling "
"water to make a cup of fruit tea."
msgstr ""
"Papierowa saszetka z liśćmi i owocami w środku. Włóż do wrzątku, by "
"przygotować kubek owocowej herbaty."

#. ~ Description of "black tea bag"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A paper sachet with tea leaves inside.  Put it into boiling water to make a "
"cup of black tea."
msgstr ""
"Papierowa saszetka z liśćmi herbaty w środku. Włóż do wrzątku, by "
"przygotować kubek czarnej herbaty."

#. ~ Description of "green tea bag"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A paper sachet with tea leaves inside.  Put it into boiling water to make a "
"cup of green tea."
msgstr ""
"Papierowa saszetka z liśćmi herbaty w środku. Włóż do wrzątku, by "
"przygotować kubek zielonej herbaty."

#. ~ Description of "piece of cardboard"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A piece of cardboard."
msgstr "Kawałek kartonu."

#. ~ Description of "cattle fodder bundle"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A pile of cattle fodder, about enough to feed a goat or a sheep for a day."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "yeast"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A powder-like mix of cultured yeast, good for baking and brewing alike."
msgstr ""
"Sproszkowany pakiet kultur drożdży przydatny w pieczeniu i gorzelnictwie."

#. ~ Description of "yogurt starter culture"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A powder-like mix of cultured yogurt bacteria, good for fermenting yogurt."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "garden snail"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A small gastropod harvested from the bushes.  These are dangerous to consume "
"raw, but could be worth cooking if you got enough of them."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "instant coffee mix"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A small packet of commercial instant coffee powder.  No creamer or sweetener "
"added."
msgstr ""
"Mały pakiet komercyjnej rozpuszczalnej kawy w proszku. Bez dodatku śmietanki "
"i słodzika."

#. ~ Description of "small plant"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A small plant or flower, edible by grazers and ruminants only.  Seeing this "
"item is a bug."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "honeydew"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A sugar-rich sticky substance, produced by aphids from plant sap.  Ants and "
"bees love it."
msgstr ""
"Bogata w cukier lepka substancja, wytwarzana przez mszyce z soków "
"roślinnych. Uwielbiają ją mrówki i pszczoły."

#. ~ Description of "swarm of bees"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A swarm of honey bees, displaced from the hive.  Without the support and "
"nutrients of an apiary, or taking root somewhere, they will die in a few "
"days."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "nut paste"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A thick mass of ground nuts that are ready to be pressed into oil."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "royal jelly"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A translucent hexagonal chunk of wax, filled with dense, milky, bitter and "
"acidic-tasting jelly.  Though some hold it as a panacea, it doesn't have any "
"medical benefit.  Still it is rich with the most beneficial substances the "
"hive can produce."
msgstr ""
"Przezroczysty heksagonalny kawałek wosku, wypełniony gęstym mlecznym żelem o "
"gorzko-kwaśnym smaku. Choć niektórzy uważają to za panaceum, to nie ma "
"żadnych właściwości medycznych. Mimo to nadal zawiera najlepsze składniki, "
"jakie tylko może wyprodukować ul."

#. ~ Description of "dried bottle gourd"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"A vegetable from the gourd family, bottle gourds were brought to the "
"Americas by the first Native American settlers crossing the Bering strait.  "
"This one has been dried for processing into a watertight container."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "akutaq"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Also called Inuit or Alaskan ice cream, this is a dense mix of solid fat and "
"sugar that makes for a sweet dessert reminiscent of cake frosting.  It is a "
"traditional food of people throughout the arctic, providing a massive amount "
"of energy to fuel a difficult lifestyle in grueling conditions."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "akutaq with fruit"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Also called Inuit or Alaskan ice cream, this is a dense mix of solid fat, "
"fruit, and sugar that makes for a sweet dessert reminiscent of cake "
"frosting.  It is a traditional food of people throughout the arctic, "
"providing a massive amount of energy to fuel a difficult lifestyle in "
"grueling conditions."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "dried soybeans"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Beige colored beans, dried until rock hard.  They'll need to be cooked or "
"processed before use."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "raw soybeans"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Beige colored beans.  They have many uses, but in their raw form are fairly "
"poisonous to humans."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "blood rice pudding"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Blood rice pudding is a pastry made from blood and rice grains.  Best with "
"chopped peanuts, but also good to eat with various seasonings."
msgstr ""
"Kaszanka z ryżem to produkt spożywczy z krwi i ziaren ryżu. Najlepiej "
"smakuje z posiekanymi orzeszkami ziemnymi, ale równie dobrze można ją jeść z "
"różnymi przyprawami."

#. ~ Description of "canned beans"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Canned beans.  A staple among canned goods, these are reputedly good for "
"one's coronary health."
msgstr ""
"Puszkowana fasola. Podstawowy produkt w gamie puszkowanych warzyw. Ma dobry "
"wpływ na zdrowie układu krążenia."

#. ~ Description of "canned tomato"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Canned tomato.  A staple in many pantries, and useful for many recipes."
msgstr ""
"Pomidory w puszce. Podstawowy zasób wielu spiżarni i użyteczny składnik "
"wielu przepisów kulinarnych."

#. ~ Description of "Kentucky coffee grounds"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Coffee grounds created through washing, cleaning, and roasting the pods from "
"a Kentucky coffeetree.  They can be used to create coffee."
msgstr ""
"Ziarna kawy powstałe z mycia, czyszczenia i prażenia owoców kłęku "
"amerykańskiego. Można z nich zrobić kawę."

#. ~ Description of "dried beans"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Dehydrated beans.  Tasty and nutritious when cooked, virtually inedible when "
"dry."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "dehydrated tofu"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Dehydrated tofu, sealed and still extra firm to last a long time."
msgstr ""
"Odwodnione tofu, szczelnie zamknięte i nadal doskonale jędrne, by posłużyło "
"na dłużej."

#. ~ Description of "powdered gelatin"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Dried and powdered gelatin, used as a gelling agent when mixed with water."
msgstr ""
"Wysuszona i sproszkowana żelatyna, używana jako czynnik żelujący po "
"zmieszaniu z wodą."

#. ~ Description of "dried earthworms"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Dried, cooked and ground earthworms."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "dry cat food"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Dry kibbles of cat food with a long shelf life.  Made from dried processed "
"meats and grains, and enriched with vitamins and minerals."
msgstr ""
"Sucha mieszanka karmy dla kotów z długim okresem przydatności do spożycia. "
"Zrobiona z przetworzonych mięs i ziaren, wzbogacona witaminami i minerałami."

#. ~ Description of "press cake"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Dry leftovers that remain after extracting the oil from nuts or seeds."
msgstr ""
"Suche resztki, które pozostają po wyciśnięciu oleju z orzechów lub nasion."

#. ~ Description of "dry dog food"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Dry morsels of dog food with a long shelf life.  Made from dried processed "
"meats and grains, and enriched with vitamins and minerals."
msgstr ""
"Sucha mieszanka karmy dla psów z długim okresem przydatności do spożycia. "
"Zrobiona z przetworzonych mięs i ziaren, wzbogacona witaminami i minerałami."

#. ~ Description of "fresh gelatin"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Fresh gelatin.  Not vegan-friendly!"
msgstr "Świeża żelatyna. Nie dla wegan!"

#. ~ Description of "extracted gelatin"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Freshly extracted gelatin in a dilute acid solution.  It needs to be "
"strained to separate the gelatin from the acid."
msgstr ""
"Świeżo pozyskana żelatyna w roztworze z rozcieńczonego kwasu. Należy ją "
"odsączyć, by oddzielić kwas od żelatyny."

#. ~ Description of "coffee powder"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Ground coffee beans.  You can boil it into a mediocre stimulant, or "
"something better if you had a coffee pot."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "candied honey"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Honey, that stuff the bees make.  The sugars have crystallized, but this "
"doesn't affect the flavor or anything."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "Mycus fruit"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Humans might call this a Gray Delicious apple: large, gray, and smells even "
"better than the Marloss.  If they didn't reject it for its alien origins.  "
"But we know better."
msgstr ""
"Ludzie mogliby ten owoc nazwać Szarym Jabłkiem, jest bowiem duży, szary i "
"pachnie lepiej niż Marloss. Gdyby tylko nie odrzucili go z uwagi na obce "
"pochodzenie. Ale ty wiesz lepiej. "

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Kentucky coffee grounds"
msgid_plural "Kentucky coffee grounds"
msgstr[0] "garść prażonych ziaren kłęku amerykańskiego"
msgstr[1] "garście prażonych ziaren kłęku amerykańskiego"
msgstr[2] "garści prażonych ziaren kłęku amerykańskiego"
msgstr[3] "garści prażonych ziaren kłęku amerykańskiego"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Marloss berry"
msgid_plural "Marloss berries"
msgstr[0] "jagoda Marloss"
msgstr[1] "jagody Marloss"
msgstr[2] "jagód Marloss"
msgstr[3] "jagody Marloss"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Marloss gelatin"
msgid_plural "Marloss gelatin"
msgstr[0] "żelatyna z Marloss"
msgstr[1] "porcje żelatyny z Marloss"
msgstr[2] "porcji żelatyny z Marloss"
msgstr[3] "porcji żelatyny z Marloss"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Mycus fruit"
msgid_plural "Mycus fruits"
msgstr[0] "owoc Grzybni"
msgstr[1] "owoce Grzybni"
msgstr[2] "owoców Grzybni"
msgstr[3] "owocu Grzybni"

#. ~ Description of "acid soaked hide"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Raw hide soaking in a dilute acid solution to extract collagen.  After 24 "
"hours the solution can be strained to extract fresh gelatin."
msgstr ""
"Surowa skóra namoczona w rozcieńczonym kwasie by wydobyć kolagen. Po 24 "
"godzinach roztwór można odsączyć, by wydobyć świeżą żelatynę."

#. ~ Description of "raw edamame"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Raw soybeans still in their pod.  They can be cooked as-is or shelled for "
"further processing, but in their raw form, they're toxic to humans."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "grass"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Some grass, edible by grazers and ruminants only.  Seeing this item is a bug."
msgstr "Trawa, pokarm dla przeżuwaczy. Jeśli widzisz ten przedmiot, to błąd."

#. ~ Description of "koji"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Some ground rice covered with a special kind of mold used for "
"saccharification and fermentation in Japanese cuisine."
msgstr ""
"Trochę zmielonego ryżu pokrytego specjalnym rodzajem pleśni używanej do "
"scukrzania i fermentacji w kuchni japońskiej."

#. ~ Description of "underbrush"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Some underbrush, edible by ruminants only.  Seeing this item is a bug."
msgstr ""
"Poszycie, pokarm dla przeżuwaczy. Jeśli widzisz ten przedmiot, to błąd."

#. ~ Description of "chewing gum"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "That gum you liked is probably not going to come back in style."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "chitin powder"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"This chitin powder can be used to craft fertilizer and some other things."
msgstr ""
"Ta mączka z chityny może się przydać do produkcji nawozu dla roślin i kilku "
"innych rzeczy."

#. ~ Description of "embalmed human brain"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"This is a human brain soaked in a solution of highly toxic formaldehyde.  "
"Eating this would be a terrible idea."
msgstr ""
"To ludzki mózg zakonserwowany w roztworze toksycznej formaliny. Zjedzenie "
"tego było by fatalne w skutkach."

#. ~ Description of "wet cat food"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"This is wet food for cats, made from canned fresh meats.  It has a pungent "
"aroma that cats seem to love."
msgstr ""
"To mokra karma dla kotów, zrobiona z puszkowanych świeżych mięs. Dziwnie "
"pachnie, ale kotom wydaje się smakować."

#. ~ Description of "wet dog food"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"This is wet food for dogs, made from canned fresh meats.  It smells strange, "
"but dogs seem to love it."
msgstr ""
"To mokra karma dla psów, zrobiona z puszkowanych świeżych mięs. Dziwnie "
"pachnie, ale psom wydaje się smakować."

#. ~ Description of "Marloss berry"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"This looks like a blueberry the size of your fist, but pinkish in color.  It "
"has a strong but delicious aroma, but is clearly either mutated or of alien "
"origin."
msgstr ""
"Wygląda jak borówka wielkości twojej pięści, ale o różowawym kolorze. Ma "
"intensywny, zachęcający zapach, ale jest albo zmutowana albo obcego "
"pochodzenia."

#. ~ Description of "Marloss gelatin"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"This looks like a handful of lemon-colored liquid which has taken a set, "
"much like pre-Cataclysm Jello.  It has a strong but delicious aroma, but is "
"clearly either mutated or of alien origin."
msgstr ""
"Kanarkowy w kolorze płyn który zastygł niemal jak galaretka sprzed "
"Kataklizmu. Ma intensywny, zachęcający zapach, ale jest albo zmutowany albo "
"obcego pochodzenia."

#. ~ Description of "tofu"
#. ~ Description of "fried tofu"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"Tofu, a soy protein crucial to East Asian cuisine.  It absorbs flavors very "
"well and can be used as a meat alternative in many dishes."
msgstr ""
"Tofu, proteina sojowa kluczowa w kuchni wschodnioazjatyckiej. Dobrze "
"absorbuje smaki i w wielu daniach jest alternatywą mięsa."

#. ~ Description of "cooked lentils"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Wet, cooked lentils.  Humble and nutrient-rich, but pretty bland."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "bird food"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"What birds eat.  Mainly made of seeds, silage or legumes.  It's perfect for "
"small birds."
msgstr ""
"Ptasia karma zrobiona z ziaren, kiszonki i roślin strączkowych. Doskonała "
"dla małych ptaków."

#. ~ Description of "cattle fodder"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid ""
"What cattle eat.  Mainly made of grass, silage or legumes.  It's perfect for "
"ruminants."
msgstr ""
"Pokarm dla bydła. Pasza złożona głównie z trawy, kiszonki lub roślin "
"strączkowych, jest doskonała dla przeżuwaczy."

