#. ~ Description of "broccoli"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A big stalk of broccoli.  It's a bit tough, but rich in Vitamin C and quite "
"delicious when properly cooked."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "handful of spinach"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A bunch of spinach leaves.  Their ability to provide one with superhuman "
"strength has been greatly exaggerated by popular media."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cut chili pepper"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A chili pepper that's been cut into pieces.  The seeds have been removed."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cut bell pepper"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A chopped up bell pepper with the seeds removed."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cut salad cucumber"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A chopped-up salad cucumber."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cut zucchini"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A chopped-up summer squash.  The seeds have been removed."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "fungal chunk"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A chunk of fungal matter.  Eating unfamiliar mushrooms is a bad idea."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "hops flower"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A cluster of small cone-like flowers, indispensable for brewing beer."
msgstr "Przypominające szyszki kwiaty chmielu, nieocenione w warzeniu piwa."

#. ~ Description of "lettuce head"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A crisp head of iceberg lettuce.  You should probably prepare it before "
"eating."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cut eggplant"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A cut-up eggplant with many of the seeds picked out."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cut tomato"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A cut-up tomato with the seeds removed."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "triffid flesh"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A dense chunk of rubbery plant matter.  Though flexible and succulent, it's "
"far too fibrous for a person to eat."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "bell pepper"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A green bell pepper.  Eating it whole and raw would be kind of a hassle, "
"considering all the seeds."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "sea lettuce"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A handful of edible green seaweed.  It makes a good snack as-is, but can be "
"dried or prepared in a number of ways."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "dandelion"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A handful of freshly-picked yellow dandelions.  In their current raw state "
"they are quite bitter."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "fiddleheads"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A handful of immature fern fronds, still curled up like the head of a "
"fiddle.  Delicious when cooked, but consuming them raw can cause food "
"poisoning."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "handful of shredded cabbage"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A handful of shredded cabbage."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "handful of shredded lettuce"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A handful of shredded iceberg lettuce."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "seaweed"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A handful of slimy seaweed.  It doesn't look edible, but properly dried, it "
"might make for decent kindling."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cabbage head"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A head of crisp white cabbage.  You should probably prepare it before eating."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "carrot"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A healthy root vegetable.  Rich in vitamin A!"
msgstr "Zdrowe warzywo z jadalnym czerwonym korzeniem. Bogate w witaminę A!"

#. ~ Description of "salsify root"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A highly nutritious root, it is tough and bland until cooked, at which point "
"it tastes strangely similar to oysters."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "tomato"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A juicy red tomato.  It gained popularity in Italy after being brought back "
"from the New World."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "pumpkin"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A large gourd, about the size of a person's head.  It'll require some "
"disassembly before use."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "horseradish root"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A large white tapered root of a horseradish plant.  Way too spicy to eat in "
"this form, but can be used for making condiments."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "bladderwrack"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A leafy bunch of seaweed covered in air bladders.  Many claims are made "
"about its health benefits, but at least as a foodstuff, it's no better or "
"worse than other edible seaweed."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cooking banana"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A much less sweet and more starchy relative of the banana; unlike dessert "
"bananas, they usually are eaten cooked rather than raw, and can be processed "
"into flour.  They are a staple food in tropical regions of the world.  Also "
"known as plantains."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "eggplant"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A normal and healthy purple eggplant.  Needs to be disassembled before being "
"useful for cooking."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "raw potato"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A potato, mildly toxic and not very tasty raw.  Delicious and filling when "
"properly cooked."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "garlic bulb"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A pungent garlic bulb, popular as a seasoning for its strong flavor.  Can be "
"disassembled into cloves or planted as is."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cut pumpkin"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A quarter section of a pumpkin.  The seeds and stringy inner pulp have been "
"removed."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "celery"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A single stalk of celery.  Neither tasty nor very nutritious, but it goes "
"well with salad."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "sugar kelp"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A sizable strip of new growth harvested from a sugar kelp.  While these are "
"most often dried, it seems edible enough as is."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "Jerusalem artichoke"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A slightly sweet tuber.  Contains much inulin which may cause some minor "
"issues with your digestive tract, so it should be cooked."
msgstr ""
"Lekko słodka bulwa. Zawiera dużo inuliny, która może powodować drobne "
"problemy z przewodem pokarmowym, dlatego należy ją gotować."

#. ~ Description of "pile of seaweed"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A slimy heap of seaweed.  It doesn't look edible, but properly dried, it "
"might make for decent kindling."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cattail rhizome"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A small tuber-like root from a cattail plant.  Its crisp white flesh is very "
"starchy and fibrous, but you really ought to cook it before you attempt to "
"eat it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "bee balm"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A snow-white flower also known as wild bergamot.  Smells faintly of mint."
msgstr ""
"Śnieżnobiały kwiatek zwany też dziką bergamotką. Ma słaby miętowy zapach."

#. ~ Description of "rhubarb"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A sour stalk of the rhubarb plant, often used in baking pies."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "chili pepper"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A spicy chili pepper.  Not the best on its own, but adds great flavor when "
"used in cooking."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "dogbane"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A stalk of dogbane.  It has very fibrous stems and is mildly poisonous."
msgstr ""
"Łodyga psitruja. Roślina ta ma bardzo włóknista łodygą i jest łagodnie "
"trującą."

#. ~ Description of "mugwort"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A stalk of mugwort.  Smells wonderful."
msgstr "Źdźbło bylicy pospolitej. Pięknie pachnie."

#. ~ Description of "cattail stalk"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A stiff, green stalk from a cattail plant.  It is starchy and fibrous, but "
"it would be much better if you cooked it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "plant stalk"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A stiff, green stalk from a plant.  It is starchy and fibrous, but it would "
"be much better if you cooked it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "zucchini"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A tasty summer squash."
msgstr "Letnie warzywo, bardzo smaczne, gdy je poddusić na ogniu."

#. ~ Description of "cotton boll"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A tough protective capsule bulging with densely-packed fibers and seeds, "
"this cotton boll can be processed into usable material with the right tools."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "raw bottle gourd"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A vegetable from the gourd family, bottle gourds were brought to the "
"Americas by the first Native American settlers crossing the Bering strait.  "
"It can be further prepared to produce a hard, watertight shell, usable as a "
"biodegradable liquid container.  Eating it doesn't look worth it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "chicory root"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A very bitter root, not meant to be eaten raw."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "wild garlic"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Also called ramps, this delicate leafy vegetable is healthy and a tasty "
"ingredient for many dishes."
msgstr ""
"To delikatne warzywo liściaste jest zdrowe i stanowi smaczny składnik wielu "
"potraw."

#. ~ Description of "handful of ground nuts"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"An almost forgotten staple of the native tribes, called the Indian potato by "
"some.  Very nutritious, but mildly toxic unless cooked."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "onion"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"An aromatic onion used in cooking.  Cutting these up can make your eyes "
"sting!"
msgstr ""
"Aromatyczna cebula to częsty składnik potraw. Kucharz płakał przy krojeniu."

#. ~ Description of "wild vegetables"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"An assortment of edible-looking wild plants.  Most are quite bitter-"
"tasting.  Some are inedible until cooked."
msgstr "Różnego sortu dzikie rośliny jadalne. Większość jest dość gorzkawa."

#. ~ Description of "burdock"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "Burdock, a bitter thistle-like vegetable.  Can be eaten raw or cooked."
msgstr ""
"Łopian, gorzkie przypominające oset warzywo. Można spożywać na surowo lub po "
"ugotowaniu."

#. ~ Description of "garlic clove"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "Cloves of garlic, useful as a seasoning."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "green tea leaves"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Dried leaves of a tropical plant.  You can boil them into green tea, or you "
"can just eat them raw.  They're pretty gross and not too filling that way, "
"though."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "black tea leaves"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Dried leaves of a tropical plant.  You can boil them into tea, or you can "
"just eat them raw.  They're pretty gross and not too filling that way, "
"though."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "grape leaves"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Edible leaves of the grape vine.  Typically used in salads or as a food "
"wrapping."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "Japanese knotweed stems"
msgid_plural "Japanese knotweed stems"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "Jerusalem artichoke"
msgid_plural "Jerusalem artichokes"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "horseradish greens"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Leaves of a horseradish plant with a sharp, bitter and peppery taste.  "
"They're edible, but not commonly eaten."
msgstr ""
"Liście chrzanu o ostrym, gorzkim i pieprznym smaku. Są jadalne, ale rzadko "
"się je jada."

#. ~ Description of "handful of bamboo shoots"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Raw woody bamboo shoots, they require some preparation before they can be "
"eaten safely."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "handful of raw beans"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Raw, uncooked beans.  They are mildly toxic to humans in this form, but you "
"could cook them to make them tasty."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "handful of chicory greens"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "Some chicory greens.  They are quite bitter but high in calcium."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "Japanese knotweed stems"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Some young Japanese knotweed stems.  They taste a bit like rhubarb and "
"contain good amounts of vitamin A.  Refreshing."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "handful of young leaves"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Some young leaves from miscellaneous plants.  They're tender enough to eat, "
"but not very tasty on their own."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "poppy pod"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"The fruit of the poppy flower, a seed-bearing head left over after the "
"petals have dropped off."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "dahlia root"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"The large, tuberous root of a dahlia flower.  It smells spicy, but is too "
"starchy to eat without cooking."
msgstr ""
"Duży bulwiasty korzeń dalii. Ma ostry zapach, ale jest zbyt bogaty w "
"skrobię, by spożywać bez gotowania."

#. ~ Description of "salad cucumber"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"The larger cousin of a pickle.  A vegetable from the gourd family.  Not "
"especially flavorful, but very refreshing."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "lotus root"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"The rhizome of the lotus, which has many tubular cavities inside, can be "
"eaten both raw and cooked."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "wild root"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"These are often wild carrots, but beware of poisonous lookalikes.  In any "
"case, the root is tough and is not as tasty as a real raw carrot."
msgstr ""
"Często są to dzikie marchewki, ale należy uważać na ich trujące "
"odpowiedniki. W każdym razie korzeń jest twardy i nie jest tak smaczny jak "
"prawdziwa, surowa marchew."

#. ~ Description of "pile of wintergreen leaves"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"These leaves smell strongly medicinal.  When chewed, they first taste sweet "
"but the aftertaste is incredibly bitter.  These leaves contain good amounts "
"of methyl salicylate and merely chewing them may have a similar effect to "
"aspirin."
msgstr ""
"Liście te mają silny leczniczy zapach. Podczas żucia najpierw smakują "
"słodko, ale później mają bardzo gorzki posmak. Liście te zawierają duże "
"ilości salicylanu metylu, a samo ich żucie może mieć działanie podobne do "
"aspiryny."

#. ~ Description of "wild sarsaparilla root"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"This aromatic rhizome can be eaten as is in an emergency, but it is much "
"better used for making beverages.  Its taste is pleasant but it is also "
"tough and stringy."
msgstr ""
"To aromatyczne kłącze może być spożywane w stanie świeżym w razie „W”, ale "
"znacznie lepiej nadaje się do produkcji napojów. Ma przyjemny smak, ale jest "
"twarde i żylaste."

#. ~ Description of "sugar beet"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"This fleshy root is ripe and flowing with sugars; it'll just take some "
"processing to extract them."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "wheat-free flour"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"This wheat-free white flour is useful for baking items for those with grain "
"intolerances."
msgstr ""

#. ~ "activation_message" action message of item "pile of wintergreen leaves"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "You chew the wintergreen leaves."
msgstr "Żujesz liście golterii."

